==French==

===Etymology===
From {{m|fr|icelui}}, from {{compound|ici|t1=here|lui|t2=him|lang=fr}} or from {{etyl|VL.|fr}} {{m|la|*eccillui}}, a compound of {{m|la|ecce}} + {{m|la|*illūi}}, itself a Vulgar Latin form of {{m|la|illī}}, dative singular of {{m|la|ille}} under the influence of {{m|la|cui}}. (see {{m|fr|lui}}). Compare Italian {{m|it|colui}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Fr-celui.ogg|audio|lang=fr}}
* {{IPA|/səlɥi/|lang=fr}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|fr|pronoun|demonstrative||plural|ceux|feminine|celle|feminine plural|celles}}

# [[the one]]
#: '''''Celui''' qui est là, c'est moi.'' The one who is there, it's me.

